        "preComments": [
          "// Pins that a stored view records every length in millimeters, whatever unit",
          "// the author wrote. More than one consumer reads these values and some become",
          "// engine commands, which are in millimeters, so one canonical unit removes a",
          "// conversion convention those consumers would otherwise have to share.",
          "//",
          "// The program memory snapshot is the assertion: 2inch is stored as 50.8, and",
          "// the inch and centimeter coordinates of each target are stored as their",
          "// millimeter equivalents. Every length written here is deliberately in a unit",
          "// other than millimeters, because a millimeter input cannot tell the two",
          "// storage conventions apart."
        ],
